    "forensics": "Four out of six losing trades (NTPC, INFY, and two in TATASTEEL) suffered identical ~0.70% gross price excursions that hit stop-losses during the low-liquidity mid-morning transition (10:25\u201311:10 IST), indicating that a 0.70% stop-loss floor is slightly too tight for high-beta NSE equities and acts as a magnet for intraday mean-reversion whipsaws. Furthermore, ICICIBANK (Trade #4) achieved a positive gross profit (+\u20b93.32) via a trailing stop but resulted in a net loss (-\u20b90.72) due to statutory transaction fees, while overall Phase 2 gross profitability (+\u20b944.20) was completely erased by \u20b946.90 in brokerage and STT/exchange charges.",
    "learning": "In small-capital NSE cash equity intraday trading, statutory fee drag requires wider minimum reward targets to expand per-trade gross expectancy, alongside maximum allowable stop-loss buffers and higher volume sweep thresholds to filter out mid-day retail noise and premature breakeven stop-outs.",
